                                {
                                    content: `<h3>Who Controls HTML?</h3>
• <b>W3C</b> (World Wide Web Consortium) - published the numbered versions.<br>
• <b>WHATWG</b> (Web Hypertext Application Technology Working Group) - formed in 2004 by browser makers.<br>
• WHATWG was created because developers felt W3C was moving toward XHTML 2.0, which broke old pages.<br>
• In <b>2019</b> W3C and WHATWG agreed that WHATWG maintains the single Living Standard.<br><br>

<h3>What is a Living Standard?</h3>
• There are no more version numbers after HTML5.<br>
• Features are added continuously as browsers implement them.<br>
• So writing HTML6 on a resume is incorrect - it does not exist.`,
                                }
