                                    content: `<h3>4. Advanced Reference - Resolution Rules</h3>
• <b>Starts with a scheme</b> - used as is, base ignored.<br>
• <b>Starts with //</b> - inherits the base scheme only.<br>
• <b>Starts with /</b> - inherits scheme, host and port; replaces the path.<br>
• <b>Starts with ?</b> - keeps the path, replaces the query.<br>
• <b>Starts with #</b> - keeps everything, replaces the fragment.<br>
• <b>Empty string</b> - the current document, without the fragment.<br>
• <b>Anything else</b> - resolved against the base's <i>directory</i>, meaning everything up to and including the last slash.<br><br>

<h3>The Directory Rule</h3>
• This is the source of the trailing slash confusion.<br>
• Base /courses has directory /, so java.html gives /java.html.<br>
• Base /courses/ has directory /courses/, so java.html gives /courses/java.html.`,
