                                    content: `<h3>1. Definition</h3>
• An <b>email link</b> is an anchor whose href starts with <b>mailto:</b> followed by an email address.<br>
• Example: &lt;a href="mailto:info@javaschoollab.com"&gt;Email us&lt;/a&gt;<br>
• Clicking it opens the default mail app with the address already filled.<br><br>

<h3>2. Purpose of This Topic</h3>
• To let a visitor contact you in one click instead of copying the address by hand.<br>
• To pre fill the subject and the body so the enquiry arrives in a useful shape.<br>
• To place a support address on a contact page or in the footer.<br><br>

<h3>3. Need of This Topic</h3>
• Typing an email address by hand causes spelling mistakes and lost enquiries.<br>
• A plain text address is not clickable on a mobile phone.<br>
• Support teams need the subject line to be consistent so tickets can be sorted.`,
