                                    content: `<h3>1. Definition</h3>
&bull; <b>srcset</b> is a <b>list of image files</b> that the browser can choose from.<br>
&bull; Each item is written as <b>file name, a space, then a descriptor</b>, and items are separated by commas.<br>
&bull; A <b>w descriptor</b> like 800w tells the real pixel width of that file.<br>
&bull; An <b>x descriptor</b> like 2x tells the screen density it is meant for.<br>
&bull; The plain <b>src</b> stays as the backup for very old browsers.<br>
<h3>2. Purpose of This Topic</h3>
&bull; To send a small file to a phone and a big file to a desktop.<br>
&bull; To send a sharp 2x file to a retina laptop and a normal file to an old monitor.<br>
&bull; To save mobile data for users on limited 4G packs.<br>
<h3>3. Need of This Topic</h3>
&bull; Downloading a 1600 pixel picture on a 360 pixel phone wastes data and time.<br>
&bull; A page that opens fast on mobile keeps customers on the site.<br>
&bull; It is asked in almost every front end interview about performance.<br>`,
