                                    content: `<h3>4. Advantages</h3>
&bull; <b>Grouping.</b> All the link regions of one picture stay in one block of code.<br>
&bull; <b>Reusable.</b> Two images can share the same map by using the same name.<br>
&bull; <b>Invisible.</b> It does not disturb the page layout in any way.<br>
&bull; <b>Native.</b> No JavaScript is needed for the linking to work.<br>
<h3>5. Disadvantages</h3>
&bull; <b>Name must be unique</b> in the whole page, and duplicates cause confusing bugs.<br>
&bull; <b>Silent failure.</b> A wrong name gives no error message, the image simply does not respond.<br>
&bull; <b>No styling.</b> You cannot highlight the map regions with CSS.<br>
&bull; <b>Ties to fixed pixels.</b> The areas inside it use fixed coordinates, so it does not scale.<br>
&bull; <b>Old technique.</b> Modern projects prefer inline svg links instead.<br>`,
