                                    content: `<h3>1. Definition</h3>
• The <b>&lt;header&gt;</b> element holds <b>introductory content</b> for a page or a section.<br>
• Typically a logo, the site title, a search box and the navigation.<br>
• It is a block element.<br><br>

<h3>2. Purpose of This Topic</h3>
• To mark the top area of a page or of a section as its introduction.<br>
• To replace the old &lt;div id="header"&gt; pattern with a tag that has real meaning.<br><br>

<h3>3. Need of This Topic</h3>
• A screen reader user needs to know where the page banner is so they can skip it.<br>
• Search engines use it to identify the site identity area.<br>
• Without it, the top of your page is just an anonymous box.`,
