                                    content: `<h3>4. Advantages</h3>
&bull; <b>Very simple grammar.</b> Only selectors, braces, colons and semicolons, so it is easy to learn in one day.<br>
&bull; <b>Forgiving.</b> An unknown property is skipped and the rest of the file still works.<br>
&bull; <b>Readable.</b> Anyone on the team can open a stylesheet and understand the structure.<br>
&bull; <b>Groupable.</b> Comma separated selectors avoid repeating the same block.<br><br>

<h3>5. Disadvantages</h3>
&bull; <b>Silent failures.</b> No error message when you make a spelling mistake.<br>
&bull; <b>A missing closing brace</b> can break every rule that follows it in the file.<br>
&bull; <b>Whitespace is not enforced,</b> so untidy files become unreadable without a formatter.<br>
&bull; <b>Values are not type checked.</b> Writing font-size: 20 without a unit simply does nothing.`,
