                                    content: `<h3>1. Definition</h3>
&bull; A &lt;style&gt; element creates a <b>render blocking</b> stylesheet that is parsed as part of the HTML document and belongs to the <b>author origin</b>.<br>
&bull; Its position in the document matters for the cascade when specificity and layer are equal, because document order breaks the tie.<br>
&bull; It participates in the CSSOM as a CSSStyleSheet, so it can be manipulated at runtime through document.styleSheets.<br><br>

<h3>2. Purpose of this topic</h3>
&bull; To implement <b>critical CSS</b> and improve Largest Contentful Paint on slow networks.<br>
&bull; To ship page scoped overrides in server rendered applications without polluting the global bundle.<br><br>

<h3>3. Need of this topic</h3>
&bull; Core Web Vitals directly affect search ranking, and eliminating a render blocking request for above the fold styles is one of the highest impact fixes.<br>
&bull; Content Security Policy environments need a nonce or hash for inline style blocks, which is an operational concern.`,
