                                    content: `<h3>4. Advantages (Advanced)</h3>
&bull; <b>Theme continuity.</b> Because inherited properties fall back to the parent, tokens and dark mode survive the reset with no extra work.<br>
&bull; <b>One primitive, many components.</b> A single <b>.reset</b> class plus composition gives buttons, links, tabs and menu items.<br>
&bull; <b>Forced colours friendly.</b> Inherited colour means Windows high contrast substitutions still reach the element.<br>
&bull; <b>Less brittle than initial.</b> It does not fight the cascade, it steps out of it politely.<br>
<h3>5. Disadvantages (Advanced)</h3>
&bull; <b>Silent display change.</b> <b>all: unset</b> sets <b>display: inline</b> which breaks flex children, grid items and hit areas, and produces no console warning.<br>
&bull; <b>box-sizing loss.</b> Global <b>box-sizing: border-box</b> is wiped on that element, so widths and paddings compute differently.<br>
&bull; <b>Semantics not restored.</b> Unlike <b>revert</b>, list markers, table layout and heading sizes stay gone.<br>
&bull; <b>Transition restart.</b> Applying <b>all</b> based resets in a state rule can cancel running transitions on unrelated properties.<br>
&bull; <b>Custom properties inherit through it</b>, so a component still receives host tokens and is not isolated.<br>`,
