                                    content: `<h3>4. Advantages</h3>
&bull; <b>Reusable</b>, write once and use on many elements.<br>&bull; <b>Combinable</b>, several classes stack on one element.<br>&bull; Stronger than a tag selector, so it overrides base styles easily.<br>&bull; Names describe intent, so the code reads clearly.<br>&bull; Works nicely with JavaScript for states like is-open and is-active.<br><h3>5. Disadvantages</h3>
&bull; The markup gets long when many utility classes are used.<br>&bull; The <b>order in the class attribute means nothing</b>, only the stylesheet order decides.<br>&bull; Class names are <b>case sensitive</b>, .Price and .price are different.<br>&bull; Careless naming causes clashes between two teams.<br>&bull; Too many tiny classes can make the HTML hard to read for beginners.<br>`,
